<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    Bead nexus-p2m1x.21 (RDR-229 P3.3c, linda's ruling 2026-11-22): idx_chunk_orphaned_at_tenant_chash, an index on nexus.chunk_orphaned_at (tenant_id, chash).

    WHY. The chunks swap adds chunk_orphaned_at_chunk_id_fk, a foreign key from chunk_orphaned_at (tenant_id, collection_id, chash, embedding_model) to the
    chunks id key with ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE. Every delete or update of a chunk row then looks up the child rows by that key, and the only index
    chunk_orphaned_at has is its name primary key (tenant_id, collection, chash), which cannot seek past collection_id: a chunk delete would read every
    orphan-clock row of the tenant. The other two children already carry an index the lookup can use (catalog_document_chunks: idx_catalog_chunks_chash
    (tenant_id, chash), catalog-001; topic_assignments: idx_ta_tenant_doc_id (tenant_id, doc_id), taxonomy-001); Rdr229SwapMovesAfterTheSwapIntegrationTest
    shows the lookup of all three on its index.

    HOW. CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY IF NOT EXISTS, in a changeset of its own with runInTransaction="false" (CONCURRENTLY cannot run inside a transaction):
    no lock a writer waits on, though the build reads the table twice. nexus.chunk_orphaned_at holds one row per chunk that lost its last owner, so it is
    small. A leftover INVALID index of this name (a build that died: the failed changeset halts that boot, and the next boot's IF NOT EXISTS would skip
    the leftover and record the changeset as run, with an index no query can use) is not replaced: the precondition counts INVALID indexes of the name and,
    with onFail="HALT" as vectors-003's collision does, keeps halting until the operator drops the leftover (DROP INDEX CONCURRENTLY, then the next boot builds
    it), so the failure the first halt reported is never silently recorded as done. onFail="CONTINUE" is not an option here: a CONTINUE changeset must not name
    a table with a foreign key into nexus.chunks (tests/test_changelog_continue_precondition_chunks_lint.py). A manually pre-built VALID index satisfies IF NOT
    EXISTS and the changeset is recorded.

    DATA EFFECT: none. The index is built over existing rows and changes no row; its maintenance cost on writes is one more btree entry per orphan-clock row.
    The number follows vectors-073 and is provisional until the final rebase. After vectors-073, before the grants-nexus-svc.xml runAlways block.
-->
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.4.xsd">

    <changeSet id="vectors-074-1" author="nexus-p2m1x.21" runInTransaction="false">
        <preConditions onFail="HALT">
            <sqlCheck expectedResult="0">SELECT COUNT(*) FROM pg_index i JOIN pg_class c ON c.oid = i.indexrelid JOIN pg_namespace n ON n.oid = c.relnamespace WHERE n.nspname = 'nexus' AND c.relname = 'idx_chunk_orphaned_at_tenant_chash' AND NOT i.indisvalid</sqlCheck>
        </preConditions>
        <comment>nexus.chunk_orphaned_at (tenant_id, chash): the child-side lookup of the chunk's id key, chunk_orphaned_at_chunk_id_fk (RDR-229 P3.3c). CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY IF NOT EXISTS, outside a transaction. DATA EFFECT: none. The rollback drops the index.</comment>
        <sql splitStatements="false" stripComments="false">
CREATE INDEX CONCURRENTLY IF NOT EXISTS idx_chunk_orphaned_at_tenant_chash
    ON nexus.chunk_orphaned_at (tenant_id, chash);
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            <sql splitStatements="false" stripComments="false">
DROP INDEX CONCURRENTLY IF EXISTS nexus.idx_chunk_orphaned_at_tenant_chash;
            </sql>
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
